# FaceChain

Face-recognition attendance with an admin dashboard. A camera script recognises
faces and reports them to a Django dashboard, which marks members present or late,
flags imposters and banned members, and shows alerts live. Attendance can also be
anchored on a local Ganache blockchain and compared against the database.

No photos are stored. Only numeric face signatures (embeddings) are saved.


## Project layout

    dashboard/      Django admin site and the API the camera script talks to
      attendance/services/
        detection.py    what happens each time a face is seen (all business rules)
        rules.py        session timing: is a session running, is someone late
        notify.py       alerts: imposters, imposter spikes, inactive members
        analytics.py    attendance, tardiness and imposter rates
        face.py         turns browser webcam frames into embeddings
        chain.py        reads attendance records from the blockchain
      attendance/static/attendance/   stylesheet and self-hosted fonts
    recognition/    Camera-side tools
      get_models.py     downloads the YuNet and SFace face models
      register.py       registers a face from the webcam (command-line fallback)
      matcher.py        compares a live face to every registered face


## Setup

Needs Python 3.12 or newer (Django 6) and a webcam for face scanning.

    cd dashboard
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    python manage.py migrate
    python manage.py createsuperuser
    python manage.py seed_demo      # optional demo data
    cd ../recognition && pip install -r requirements.txt
    python get_models.py            # needed for the face scan
    cd ../dashboard && python manage.py runserver

Then open http://127.0.0.1:8000 and sign in with the superuser you created.
The Django admin is at /admin/.


## Using it

1. Sessions: create the weekly sessions, each with a day, start time and end time.
2. Members: register a member and assign them to a session.
3. Scan: the Members page opens a browser face scan right after registering.
   If the browser camera is unavailable, use the fallback:

       cd recognition
       python register.py <member_id>

4. Dashboard: watch today's attendance, unread alerts and recent activity.
   The page refreshes itself every 5 seconds.
5. Settings & analytics: view rates over 7, 30 or 90 days and adjust the rules.


## How a detection is handled

Every face the camera reports goes to `detection.process_detection`:

| Seen | Result |
|---|---|
| Unregistered face | Recorded as an imposter. Alerts if a session is running, and a separate alert fires on a spike of imposters. |
| Banned member | Recorded as banned and raises an alert. Banned members stay in the recognition set so they can be flagged. |
| Member in their own session | Marked present once per day, and late if they arrive after the grace period. |
| Member outside their session | Recorded at most once an hour, and does not count as attendance. |

Members who miss several sessions in a row raise an inactivity alert.

These values can be changed on the Settings page:

| Setting | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Late grace minutes | 10 | Minutes after the start before someone counts as late |
| Early window minutes | 15 | How early before the start attendance is accepted |
| Imposter spike count | 5 | Unregistered faces needed to trigger a spike alert |
| Imposter spike minutes | 30 | The time window for that count |
| Inactive sessions threshold | 3 | Missed sessions in a row before an inactivity alert |


## Configuration

All of these are optional environment variables.

| Variable | Default | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| `ATTENDANCE_API_TOKEN` | `dev-token-change-me` | Shared secret between the dashboard and camera scripts. Set the same value on both sides. |
| `DASHBOARD_URL` | `http://127.0.0.1:8000` | Where the recognition scripts find the dashboard |
| `GANACHE_URL` | `http://127.0.0.1:7545` | Ganache RPC address |
| `CONTRACT_ADDRESS` | empty | Deployed attendance contract. The chain shows as offline until this is set. |
| `CONTRACT_ABI_PATH` | `blockchain/Attendance.abi.json` | Contract ABI file |

The time zone is set to Africa/Lusaka in `dashboard/config/settings.py`.


## API

These endpoints are for the camera scripts. Each request needs this header:

    Authorization: Token <ATTENDANCE_API_TOKEN>

| Method and path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/attendance/` | Report a detection |
| `GET /api/embeddings/` | Download every registered face, including banned members |
| `GET /api/members/<member_id>/face/` | Check that a member exists |
| `POST /api/members/<member_id>/face/` | Save embeddings, as `{"embeddings": [[...128 floats], ...]}` |

Body for reporting a detection. Use `null` for `member_id` when the face is unknown:

    {"member_id": "202400004", "confidence": 0.71, "tx_hash": "0x...", "block_number": 12}


## Tests

    cd dashboard
    python manage.py test attendance
    python -m flake8 attendance


## Current status

- The dashboard, rules, alerts, analytics and face registration all work.
- The live camera loop is not in the repo yet. `matcher.py` has the matching helpers,
  but nothing runs the camera and posts to `/api/attendance/`. Until it exists, you
  can test by posting to that endpoint directly.
- The `blockchain/` folder (contract and ABI) is not in the repo yet. The Blockchain
  page shows "Not connected" until it is deployed and configured.


## Before deploying

The defaults in `dashboard/config/settings.py` are for local development only:

- Set `DEBUG = False`, fill in `ALLOWED_HOSTS` and replace `SECRET_KEY`.
- Set a strong `ATTENDANCE_API_TOKEN`.
- Set `STATIC_ROOT` and run `python manage.py collectstatic`, because styles and fonts
  are static files.
- Serve over HTTPS, since browsers only allow camera access on secure pages
  (localhost is the exception).


